:: place.player-home [place hub]
@hub player_home
You are back in the privacy of your four walls.

@choicegroup bedroom-menu "Bedroom"

  @choice rest "Go to Bed" -> menu.player.home.rest
    @preview energy 1 "++Energy"
  @endchoice

@endchoicegroup

@choicegroup activity-menu "Activities"
@choice lift-weights "Lift weights" -> @exit
  @time 5m
  @when not daily.home_weightlifting
  @change skill strength 0.1
  @effect daily-flag home_weightlifting true
@endchoice
@endchoicegroup

@choicegroup bathroom-menu "Bathroom"

@choice shower "Take a shower" -> @exit
  @time 15m
  @change stat hygiene +50
  @change stat energy -5
@endchoice

@endchoicegroup


:: menu.player.home.rest -> @exit
  @passage rest-menu
  @choicegroup sleep-menu "Set your alarm to:"

You set your alarm and climb into bed. The soft sheets and warm blankets are a welcome comfort.
How long will you sleep for?

@choice sleep-8h "8 hours" -> .wake-up
  @time 8h rest
  @effect stat hygiene -5
@endchoice

@choice sleep-7h "7 hours" -> .wake-up
  @time 7h rest
  @effect stat hygiene -4.5
@endchoice

@choice sleep-6h "6 hours" -> .wake-up
  @time 6h rest
  @effect stat hygiene -4
@endchoice

@choice sleep-5h "5 hours" -> .wake-up
  @time 5h rest
  @effect stat hygiene -3.5
@endchoice

@choice sleep-4h "4 hours" -> .wake-up
  @time 4h rest
  @effect stat hygiene -3
@endchoice

@choice sleep-3h "3 hours" -> .wake-up
  @time 3h rest
  @effect stat hygiene -2.5
@endchoice

@choice sleep-2h "2 hours" -> .wake-up
  @time 2h rest
  @effect stat hygiene -2
@endchoice

@choice sleep-1h "1 hour" -> .wake-up
  @time 1h rest
  @effect stat hygiene -1.5
@endchoice

@endchoicegroup

@next "Leave" -> @exit



@passage wake-up

Your alarm goes off.
@if player.energy >= 80
  You feel well-rested, and you quickly shake off the last remnants of sleepiness.
@elseif player.energy >= 50
  You feel a little groggy, but you manage to get out of bed.
@else
  You feel exhausted, and you wish you'd slept longer. You drag yourself out of bed and get ready for the day.
@endif

@next -> @exit
